WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.247
In under two minutes, you will close voting and announce the winners.

00:00:04.247 --> 00:00:05.346
We start on the map.

00:00:06.246 --> 00:00:09.532
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:14.010
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.509
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.509 --> 00:00:17.860
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.232
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:22.928
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.706
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.706 --> 00:00:29.860
See the three dots?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.380
Tap them.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.622
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:37.507 --> 00:00:38.104
Tap Mine.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.957
These are the contests you run.

00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:43.562
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:43.562 --> 00:00:44.850
This is your dashboard.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.495
Tap Results.

00:00:47.495 --> 00:00:50.093
It shows who would win if you announced today.

00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:54.421
Tap Download results to save a spreadsheet.

00:00:56.687 --> 00:01:00.344
When voting is over, tap Close voting and announce winners.

00:01:02.154 --> 00:01:05.725
It asks you to tap again, because this cannot be undone.

00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:06.602
Tap it again.

00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:07.855
Everyone is emailed.

00:01:09.912 --> 00:01:13.302
To see what everyone sees, tap See it as voters do.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.993
The winners keep a crown on the contest page.

00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:22.728
Next up: Read your contest activity.
